EVM-Quantum-Vault — source provenance

This project contains adaptations of MIT-licensed protocol, contract and
cryptographic client code from:
  Aegis Protocol — https://github.com/imadegoodstuff/aegis-protocol
  Commit: 71e4070ff7ce56a23e66a2bf742ace889868aa50
  Copyright (c) 2026 Aegis Protocol contributors

The retained design is CCHS-K-20: Winternitz one-time signatures, a two-layer
Merkle hypertree and verifier-side subtree caching. The Solidity verifier and
state machine derive from evm/src/AegisCCHSK.sol and AegisCCHSBase.sol. The
factory is simplified from the upstream factory interface. The TypeScript
signature core derives from wallet/src/aegis cryptographic modules used by
the upstream MIT SDK; upstream sdk/package.json and sdk/README.md identify
that SDK as MIT. Upstream's GPL-3.0 wallet UI is not included.

This project changes the project/account derivation namespace, signature
digest domains, supported networks, factory interface, index storage
discipline and user interface. It is an independent project and makes no
claim of upstream endorsement. The original MIT notice is preserved in
LICENSE and src/crypto/UPSTREAM-LICENSE.txt.

The EVM-Quantum-Vault public name does not change existing protocol constants,
contract names, key derivation domains, database identifiers or backup formats.
Those identifiers retain their original values for compatibility.

No upstream SPHINCS+ C13 vendor verifier, Solana adapter, other-chain adapter,
hybrid account, browser extension or GPL wallet component is included.

Third-party npm dependencies retain their own licenses and copyright notices.
The lockfile identifies their pinned versions. Distribution of dependencies
must preserve the applicable notices; this LICENSE does not relicense them.

Experimental software. No independent security audit or proof of the complete
implementation is claimed. The protocol's one-time-key restrictions remain
essential even when a transaction is dropped or never broadcast.
